This study examines the differential decay rate for the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ process, focusing on the $q^2$ dependence of the form factors $f_1$, $f_2$, and $f_3$. Utilizing the $B_s^0$ meson sample from the LHCb detector, we analyze the decay rate across the $q^2$ range of 0.00 to 19.00 GeV$^2$. Our findings indicate that the form factors $f_1$, $f_2$, and $f_3$ exhibit a linear dependence on $q^2$ within this interval. Consequently, we propose a linear parameterization for these form factors, which offers a more straightforward description of the $q^2$ dependence compared to the BGL and CLN parameterizations. This linear approach is particularly advantageous for future analyses involving $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}\mu^{+}
u_{\mu}$ decays. Additionally, we derive the values of the CKM matrix element $|V_{cs}|$ and the product $|V_{cs}|f_1(0)$ using both the linear and CLN parameterizations. The resulting $|V_{cs}|$ values are $0.977\pm 0.012\pm 0.010$ (linear) and $0.977\pm 0.012\pm 0.010$ (CLN), while the $|V_{cs}|f_1(0)$ values are $0.977\pm 0.012\pm 0.010$ (linear) and $0.977\pm 0.012\pm 0.010$ (CLN), respectively. These results align with those obtained from the $B_s^0ightarrow D_s^{*-}	au^{+}
